#   race the rest of the binary); the parent asserts the child ran exactly that
#   test and passed, and nothing outside the child initialises the list.
#   * client_ip_resolves_the_rightmost_untrusted_hop — single hop, client-first
#     multi-hop, spoofed prefix, two trusted hops + junk, whitespace/empty
#     entries, malformed entries (incl. the port case), IPv6 and IPv4-mapped
#     normalisation, all-trusted chain → peer (with and without port), X-Real-Ip
#     fallback and precedence, untrusted peer ignoring headers, no peer, and the
#     display/client_ip byte-equality loop (13 cases × include_port ∈ {false,
#     true}), including the named multi-hop-with-trusted-prefix assertion.
#   * spoofed_prefix_cannot_choose_the_rate_limit_key — three spellings of one
#     chain are ONE key, and one key is one budget (second request through any
